#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# Differential equations

#% text
# `d_solve` solves ordinary and partial differential equations symbolically; `d_solve_value` returns the solution as an expression, and `n_dsolve` solves numerically when there is no closed form. Derivatives are written with primes: `y'(x)`, `y''(x)`.

#% section
# Symbolic solutions

#% text
# The result is a list of solutions. A general solution has constants `c(1)`, `c(2)`; initial conditions are equations in the list.

#% cell
d_solve(y'(x) == y(x), y(x), x)
#% output
#= [[y(x) -> c(1)*exp(x)]]

#% cell
d_solve([y'(x) == y(x), y(0) == 2], y(x), x)
#% output
#= [[y(x) -> 2*exp(x)]]

#% cell
d_solve(y''(x) + y(x) == 0, y(x), x)
#% output
#= [[y(x) -> c(1)*cos(x) + c(2)*sin(x)]]

#% cell
d_solve([y''(x) + y(x) == 0, y(0) == 1, y'(0) == 0], y(x), x)
#% output
#= [[y(x) -> cos(x)]]

#% text
# `d_solve_value` gives the solution itself rather than rules, and can evaluate it.

#% cell
d_solve_value([y'(x) == 2*y(x), y(0) == 1], y(x), x)
#% output
#= exp(2*x)

#% cell
d_solve_value([y'(x) == 2*y(x), y(0) == 1], y(1), x)
#% output
#= exp(2)

#% text
# A system lists the unknown functions.

#% cell
d_solve([x'(t) == y(t), y'(t) == -x(t), x(0) == 1, y(0) == 0], [x(t), y(t)], t)
#% output
#= [[x(t) -> cos(t), y(t) -> -sin(t)]]

#% section
# Numerical solutions

#% text
# `n_dsolve(eqs, y, [t, t0, t1])` returns rules with an interpolating function; use `rewrite` to evaluate it.

#% cell
sol = n_dsolve([y'(t) == y(t)^2 - t, y(0) == 0.5], y, [t, 0, 2])

#% cell
rewrite(y(2), sol)
#% output
#= -0.9957138427589801

#% section
# Common mistakes

#% item
# Initial conditions belong inside the list of equations, not as an extra argument.

#% item
# Products of unknown functions need `*`: `x(t)*y(t)`. `x(t) y(t)` and `x(t)(28 - z(t))` read as calls.

#% item
# Name the unknown as `y(x)` to get rules `y(x) -> ...`, or as `y` to get a function `y -> (x => ...)`.

#% cell
d_solve(y'(x) == y(x), y, x)
#% output
#= [[y -> (x => exp(x)*c(1))]]

#% section
# Related functions

#% text
# `d_solve`, `d_solve_value`, `n_dsolve`, `n_dsolve_value`, `rewrite`, `laplace_transform`
